Key Performance Indicators (KPIs)

1. Overview

The system provides analytical KPIs to help the Admin monitor restaurant sales and operational performance over a selected period.

The KPIs are calculated from order data stored in the Data Warehouse after the weekly data transfer from the operational database.

2. Sales KPIs
   2.1 Total Orders

Definition:
The total number of orders placed during the selected period.


2.2 Total Revenue

Definition:
The total revenue generated from accepted orders during the selected period.


2.3 Average Order Value (AOV)

Definition:
The average revenue generated per accepted order.


3.1 Accepted Orders

Definition:
The number of orders accepted by the Cashier during the selected period.

3.2 Rejected Orders

Definition:
The number of orders rejected by the Cashier during the selected period.

3.3 Acceptance Rate

Definition:
The percentage of submitted orders that were accepted by the Cashier.


3.4 Rejection Rate

Definition:
The percentage of submitted orders that were rejected by the Cashier.


4.1 Top-Selling Products

Shows the products with the highest number of units sold during the selected period.

4.2 Popular Categories

Shows the categories generating the highest number of ordered items during the selected period.

4.3 Product Sales

Shows the number of units sold and revenue generated by each product.

5. Trend Analysis
   5.1 Orders Over Time

Displays the number of orders over the selected period to identify changes in ordering activity.

5.2 Revenue Over Time

Displays revenue trends over the selected period.

